      **Inheritance**
->This is the concept whereby one class (child) acquires / inherits / borrow properties from another class (parent)-> it allows reuse to code instead of rewritting everything everything from scratch

->Parent class -> The class from which propersties are inherited -> also refered to as Base class / Super class

->Child class -> The class inheriting properties from another class -> Also referred to as Derived class /Sub class

Why use Inheritance>
1.Avoids duplicated code
2.Adds new feature to an existing class
3.Allows behaviour modification - method overriding

Types of inheritance:
1.Single inheritance - a child class inherits from a single parent class
2.Multiple inheritance - a child inherits from more than one class
3.Multilevel inheritance - a child class inherits from a parent and the parent also from another class
4.Hierrachial inheritance - multiple child classes from a single parent class

Method Overriding -> This is where a child class provides its own implementation of a method that already exeists in the parent class->The child's ,Method replaces the parent method when by a child object -> This is part of the POLYMORPHISIM concept


