*instead if returning raw data in our routes, we instead return / render full html pages and the subsequently render data in those pages 
*To render return / html pages in Flask we use a function called render_template which is imported from Flask
*The render_template() function takes as an argument the name of a html file in string format e.g. render_template("index.html")




TEMPLATE INHERITANCE
-> A mechanism of reducing redundancy in creating html files by having one base template which contains all common html components e.g navbar, footer -> Uses Jinja syntax -> Create one base template -> base.html, layout.html -> Have the other html files inherit common features from it


{% extends 'base.html'%} -->in herits features from base template {% block title %}
{% endblock %} ---> Where to put my title for child {% block content %}
{% endblock %} --> block where you place each page's unique content


